<body>
<div dir=3D"auto">Hi Allison,</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Thank you again for taking the time to speak with me. I=
=92ve reflected on our conversation and want to offer some additional conte=
xt for the record=97both to clarify key points and to express concern about=
 how some of what I shared may be interpreted.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Throughout our conversation, I sensed a familiar pattern=
=97where thoughtful, human interactions were being reframed post hoc as =93=
inappropriate=94 or =93concerning.=94 That reframing is not new to me. I ex=
perienced it often during my time at Honeyman,
 and it appeared again during our call. I want to be transparent about what=
 I witnessed, and how it continues to shape my understanding of the institu=
tional dynamics at play.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Some moments I feel are important to emphasize:</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">Ryan telling me to &quot;eat glass&quot; during our March=
 5 meeting was not a miscommunication=97it was inappropriate and aggressive=
. What I did not mention in the call, but now want to add, is that he used =
this same phrase in the Welcome Center the very
 first time he confronted me. That makes it a pattern. I have reason to bel=
ieve this is not an isolated incident.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">At the end of that March 5 meeting, Ryan spent five minut=
es repeating that =93I could just leave=94 if I felt uncomfortable. That wa=
sn=92t support=97it was pressure. The interaction felt coercive and deeply =
unprofessional. And you can hear it clearly
 in his tone.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">Logan=92s behavior, including doing stretches in front of=
 me during a long shift at the Welcome Center, created discomfort and blurr=
ed boundaries. As a new volunteer, I didn=92t know how to respond appropria=
tely to a situation where I felt my professionalism
 was being tested by someone in a position of authority.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">Logan also told me that Ranger Leaf would train me, a com=
mitment he&nbsp;never followed through on=97Leaf had no knowledge of it. Th=
at breach was the final breakdown of trust in what was already a fragile dy=
namic.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">Ryan admitted in our meeting that he never gave me the be=
nefit of the doubt, beginning with my initial interaction with Kati. That a=
dmission confirms the feeling I carried throughout my time at Honeyman: tha=
t I was being judged through a fixed
 lens, regardless of my conduct.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">The journal incident was misrepresented. My comment to th=
e ranger assistant=97&quot;not all rangers are helpful&quot;=97was not a cr=
iticism of staff. It was an appeal to ensure the journal was not ignored in=
 the lost and found. As someone who has been homeless,
 I know the emotional significance of a journal, and I was simply asking th=
at extra care be taken.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<ul data-editing-info=3D"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}" style=
=3D"list-style-type: disc;">
<li>
<div dir=3D"auto">The issue of guest perception was related to my early tex=
t message to Kati when the power went out. My statement that =93I own this =
problem in the eyes of guests=94 was not a misunderstanding of my role. It =
was an accurate reflection of how guests
 see park hosts=97as the first point of contact. My message was about optic=
s, not blame or misalignment.</div>
</li></ul>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">The common thread in all of this, and what I believe is t=
he real issue, is how I=92ve held leadership accountable in writing. The pr=
imary concern Ryan raised in that March 5 meeting was not my behavior=97it =
was my emails. The vast majority of that
 meeting centered on my written communication, which I=92ve always approach=
ed with clarity and intent. The discomfort, in my view, stemmed not from wh=
at I said=97but from the fact that I said it in a format that created a rec=
ord. This is an undeniable pattern that
 strikes at the heart of accountability and transparency.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Additionally, I want to acknowledge something I did not b=
ring up on the call: I am aware of at least three other volunteers who have=
 had similar challenges with Ryan. His behavior is not isolated. His approa=
ch to volunteers appears to follow
 a consistent pattern. I raise this not to accuse, but to suggest that what=
 I experienced fits into a broader pattern that may be worth further attent=
ion.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I=92m not sharing this to escalate or attack, but to ensu=
re that the story doesn=92t get flattened into something it never was. I=92=
ve remained calm, communicative, and reflective throughout my time in this =
program. I=92ve adapted, learned, and tried
 to contribute with sincerity and care. If there are aspects of my communic=
ation style that feel different, that is not a threat=97it=92s a strength. =
And it should not be weaponized to create distance or distrust.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">All I ask is that this be viewed with honesty and fairnes=
s. I am not asking for special treatment=97just integrity in how this is he=
ld and assessed.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">The integrity of any volunteer program depends not only o=
n the contributions of its volunteers=97but on the willingness of leadershi=
p to be accountable when trust is compromised.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Please include this message in my file as part of the ong=
oing review.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Warm Regards,</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Sam White</div>
